msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** CPU time is the post-processing time. The three mirror circuits "
"were submitted together in one run, so the recorded QPU and CPU times are "
"for all three circuits together. Each Clifford circuit run contained nine "
"PUBs with different circuit depths, so the recorded times are for all nine "
"PUBs together. Each Ising circuit run contained 10 PUBs with different "
"numbers of Trotter steps, so the recorded times are for all 10 PUBs "
"together.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the mirror circuits, the benchmarks use the RealAmplitudes, TwoLocal, "
"and EfficientSU2 ansätze with 30, 35, and 40 qubits, respectively. The "
"observables consist of a single Pauli-$Z$ operator on a randomly selected "
"qubit, with an ideal expectation value of 1.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the Clifford circuits, the benchmarks use 50- and 100-qubit circuits "
"with observables initialized as one or more randomly positioned Pauli-$Z$ "
"operators. Operator evolution increases the Pauli weight of these "
"observables, which provides more complex observables for benchmarking. The "
"observables are constructed to have an ideal expectation value of 1, which "
"is independently verified with stabilizer simulation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the Trotterized 2D tilted-field Ising (TFI) Hamiltonian simulations, the"
" benchmarks use three parameter regimes: small angle "
"$(\\theta_X,\\theta_Z,\\theta_{ZZ})=(0.1,0.1,0.1)$, near-Clifford "
"$(0.1,0.05,1.5708)$, and chaotic $(0.53,0.1,1.0)$. The observable is the "
"average magnetization,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"O_M = \\frac{1}{M}\\sum_i Z_i,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $M$ is the number of qubits in the simulation. Ideal expectation "
"values are computed with sparse Pauli dynamics (SPD), a Pauli propagation "
"method, and are validated against Qiskit statevector simulations for "
"circuits with fewer than 29 qubits.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For all benchmarks, mitigation accuracy is calculated as\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Accuracy}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\left(\n"
"1-\n"
"\\frac{\n"
"\\left|\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}-\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{mitigated}}\\right|\n"
"}{\n"
"\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}\n"
"}\n"
"\\right)\\times100\\%,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}$ and $\\langle "
"O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{mitigated}}$ are the ideal and mitigated expectation "
"values, respectively.\n"
msgstr ""

