#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example 3: Verify zero QPU overhead with LTM AI-QEM {#example-3-verify-zero-"
"qpu-overhead-with-ltm-ai-qem}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This example shows that the LTM AI-QEM function doesn't use any extra QPU "
"time. That is, LTM AI-QEM uses no more QPU time than the Estimator "
"primitive. The example again uses the mirror circuit, this time with two "
"types of PUBs. In the first type, called the commuting type, all of the "
"Pauli observables commute with each other. In the second type, called the "
"non-commuting type, none of the Pauli observables commute with each other.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each type, the observables are defined in two ways: as a list of Pauli "
"operators (`list_of_commuting` and `list_of_non_commuting`), and as a single"
" `SparsePauliOp` object that represents the sum of all the Pauli operators "
"in the list (`sum_of_commuting` and `sum_of_non_commuting`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The commuting type takes less time than the non-commuting type, because "
"Qiskit groups the commuting Pauli operators and measures them in the same "
"measurement setting. The example shows that a run with the LTM AI-QEM "
"function uses the same QPU time as a run with the IBM Quantum `EstimatorV2` "
"primitive.\n"
msgstr ""

